	title 'Desk Manager--NDA Calls'************************************************************************ Desk Manager  * for the Apple II GS** original CDA code by John Worthinton.* original NDA code by Steven Glass** Additions and alterations by Steven Glass and* Konstantin Othmer** 5.x work by Harry Yee and Mensch** System 6.0 work by Dave Lyons** This file contains**	SystemEvent*	CheckNDAStuff*	CallCDAMenu*	InstallNDA*	OpenNDA*	CloseNDA*	CloseNDAByWinPtr*	CloseAllNDAs2*	DoCloseStuff*	SystemTask*	SystemClick*	SystemEdit*	FixAppleMenu2*	GetNumNDAs*	DeskUtils*	FindThisWindow*	AreWeTop*	SendAction*	SendOpen*	SendClose*	SendInit*	StartNDACall*	EndNDACall*	AddToRunQ*	RemoveFromRunQ*	ExecuteRunItem*	RemoveNDA*	GetDeskAccInfo	DAL*	CallDeskAcc	DAL*	GetDeskGlobal	DAL**********************************************************************************************************************************************			         **	Copyright (C) 1985-1989	         **	All Rights Reserved		         **	Apple Computer, Inc.	         **			         *********************************************************************************************************************************************** Change History** 19 Feb 89 	Steven Glass** Made this work with resource manager.** 15 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Added FrontToAX to call front window for other routines.  Saved* lots of calls.** SystemClick selects window if grow clicked in back window* instead of growing.** 3/16/89	Mensch* Added stilldown call to clickinDrag routine, selecting the window was* occuring too slowly, and there was enough time to click somewhere else* before draw was being called.** 19 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Fixed bug in SystemEdit where return code from DA was trashed while * restoring the resource manager's user id.** 02 Jun 89	Steven Glass** Fixed bugs relating to re-entrancy.  When the desk manager* is re-entered the handle is locked and unlocked, leaving the first* entry with a dangling pointer.  We now inc a counter and dec a * counter so that the unlock only occurs when the counter gets to zero.** 28 Aug 89	Harry Yee* Fixed bugs relating to fix made 02 Jun 89. The counter thats inc'ed* is done in routine DerefNDAList and dec'ed in UnlockNDAList. This * counter gets imbalanced on occasion because the routines GetNumNDAs,* AddtoRunQ, and RemoveFromRunQ call DerefNDAList but not UnlockNDAList.* I now make sure both calls are made. BRC #52333. This fixes the * problem for ROM 01 machines but not for ROM 03. Fix must be made in* the desk mgr patch file.** 15 Feb 90	Harry Yee* Fix bug in RemoveNDA. The ptr PtrToThisOne was being used to keep track* of where the next NDA was to be moved to. This ptr was never updated * during each iteration of the loop that moved all NDAs up one position.** 17-Sep-90	Dave Lyons* Removed dependency on all.macros.** 20..25-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Changed FixAppleMenu (procedure now named FixAppleMenu2) to insert* the NDA items in alphabetical order if bit 0 of battery RAM location* $5F is set.* Put back all.macros.** 27-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Made sorting ignore leading blanks (GetNamePointer skips past them).** 30-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Changed CompareTwo to return CLC for equal names, so it doesn't hang* if there are two identically-named NDAs.** 3-Jan-90	Dave Lyons** Changed SystemEvent so that Apple-w or Apple-W with a System* window in front calls CloseNDAByWinPtr and returns TRUE, instead* of letting the DA or the application handle the Apple-W.** 19-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Changed FindThisWindow to examine the Aux Wind Info & fetch an* NDA Structure pointer from there.  This works pretty dang well!* Didn't have to modify the other things that call it.** New call GetDeskGlobal.  For selector 0, returns the pointer of* the last window the Desk Manager examined.  Other selectors return* error $0520.** 11-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Implementing GetDeskAccInfo and CallDeskAcc.** 17-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Removed GetWKind call from SystemEvent; now I look directly at the* window record instead, since GetWKind was changing some Window Mgr* direct page stuff.  This was very bad if SystemEvent got called* from within a window manager call, and it was making DragWindow* always drag the front window!** 21-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Changed SystemTask to return with no error if GS/OS is busy.* Changed SystemClick to honor the qContent bit of a system window* (if set, click is passed to the NDA after it is selected).** 2-May-91	Dave Lyons** After CloseAllNDAs closes true NDAs, now it goes through open* windows closing any remaining system windows (by calling* CloseNDAByWinPtr).** 10-May-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed CloseAllNDAs logic so that getting an error on CloseNDAByWinPtr* on a non-NDA system window does not cause an infinite loop!  This* was causing a hang with Video Keyboard open.** 4-Jul-91	Dave Lyons** Modified SystemClick so the first thing is does is offer to let the* NDA handle the event completely, by calling CallDeskAcc with action* code 10.** 24-Jul-91	Dave Lyons** FixAppleMenu calls SendRequest($051E=systemSaysFixedAppleMenu) after* it's done.** 9-Aug-91	Dave Lyons** OpenNDA now preserves the current port and sets the "standard" QD* port.** 16-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** FixAppleMenu now checks RealDeskStatus to see if we're started up;* if not, it tries DeskStartUp.  If we're *still* not started up, then* no NDA items are added to the Apple menu.** 17-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Small changes to support moving calls into Tool.Setup.** 11-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** Added a WindStatus check in the Command-W handling.** 9-Nov-91	Dave Lyons** Changed default minimum-size for a system window (when the system* calls GrowWindow) to width=78, height=34.** 4-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** When SystemClick handles a click on a non-front system window that has* the fQContent bit set, after the window comes to the front SystemClick* calls FindWindow to see what part of the window the click is really in.* (To see the result, try clicking in the close box of a not-in-front system* window with the fQContent bit set, like Control Panels 2.0 or an individual* control panel window.  Now it closes.  Before, the event got passed to the* system window's Action routine, which was not prepared to handle it.* Typically it just called TaskMasterDA, which would track the close box, but* nobody would close the window.)** 12-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** When SystemEvent sees a Command-W and a system window is in front, it* now uses CallDeskAcc to pass action $000B, giving the NDA a chance to* handle the key itself before forcibly calling CloseNDAbyWinPtr.************************************************************************* 26-Jun-92	Dave Lyons for 6.0.1** Changed SendAction to allow stack-based action rouines.  If you set* bit 31 of the action routine pointer, we push the stuff on the stack* so you can write in Pascal or whatever.**   function MyActionProc(code: integer; data:long): integer;** 2-Jul-92	Dave Lyons** When you OpenNDA sees the NDA is already open (has a window pointer),* it tries sending a CallDeskAcc(reOpenAction=$000C).  If the DA takes* that and puts a $0001 in the word pointed to by XY, OpenNDA takes no* further action (otherwise it calls SelectWindow).***********************************************************************	include 'all.macros'	include '::sys.equs.asm'	include 'Desk.Equates.asm'	include 'e16.memory';=================================================;; Special Macros;;=================================================	MACRO&lab	movelong &src,&dest&lab	lda &src	sta &dest	lda &src+2	sta &dest+2	mend	title 'Desk Manager--desk/DESK.SRC'******************************************************************* System Event**         result  :	 boolean     (word)*         mods    :	 modifiers   (long)*         where   :	 point       (long)*         when    :	 long*         message :	 long*         what   :	 event code  (word)*   SP->** Apologies to those who follow but we had to perform a little* kludge here.  The	ChoseCDA routine in	ROM does a silly thing* to decide how to get input.  It loads	the address of an* input routine decrements it once and does an RTS.  This* address unfortunatley is setup by SystemEvent.  With this* patch, SystemEvent is not in the same	bank and does not* know the addresses of the input routines.** So what do I do?	Well the input routine not to use has its* address in the variable KeyINput.  It	is easy to save and* restore it without caring what it is.	 The routine that* we need to use is	$D bytes after the routine not to use.** Without knowing where it is I can guarentee that the routine* will not change size or relative position in future ROMs.** Thus I calculate the address of the routine to use by adding* $D to the address	of the routine not to use.** This routine also	has to prevent multiple entries into the* CDA menu.  I do this by checking a flag on entry.  If this* flag is non zero we skip the work.  If the flag is zero,* we set the flag to non zero and bring	up the menu.  When* we return from the menu, we set the flag back to zero.** Modification History** 01 Oct 87    Steven Glass** Routine rewritten	to run in ROM.*** 31 Mar 88	Steven Glass** This code now checks to see if the CDA menu is active before* trying to pass events to NDAs.** 12/5/89	Mensch** Added code so that system event does not claim certain keyboard events. This allows* DA's to accept certain menu key equivalents.*****************************************************************	EXPORT SystemEventSystemEvent	PROC EXPORT	DefineStackOrigD	wordDAPtr	longDAHandle	longprocstat	byteret1	block 3ret2	block 3swhat	wordsmessage	longswhen	longswhere	longsmods	wordresult	wordSizeOfMonKeyIn	equ $D	php	; turn off interrupts because	sei	; dahandler expects	them off	phy	; save handle to data structure	pha	; on stack (value from WAP table)	phy	; save again to make room for	pha	; pointer.	phd	; save direct page	tsc	; get stack pointer	tcd	; make it direct		stz Result	; assume that we will not handle this event	lda swhat	; get the event type	cmp #$000A	; is it a DA event	beq ItsNDAEvent	;-------------------------------------------------;; Look at the NotAgain flag.  If it is set,; we cannot send events to an NDA.;	jsr LocalDeref	ldy #o_NotAgain	lda [DAPtr],y	bne CannotGoOn		brl CheckNDAStuff	; No, move on.ItsNDAEvent;-------------------------------------------------;; It is a DA event.	 We will have to try to call; the CDA menu but...;;; Calling SaveScrn clobbers the important variable; NumInts.  So I save NumInts here and restore it; below.;	sep #$30	lda >NumInts	; get num ints and	pha	rep #$30;-------------------------------------------------;; Look at the NotAgain flag.  If it is set,; we cannot do this	again.;	jsr LocalDeref	ldy #o_NotAgain	lda [DAPtr],y	bne SkipThisOne;-------------------------------------------------;; Set the KeyInput field so that right routine; is called.  (Save	orig KeyInput on stack.);	lda >keyinput	pha	clc	adc #SizeofMonKeyIn	sta >keyinput;-------------------------------------------------;; Zero the Active flag so that we do not send; keystrokes to NDA's on screen that cannot be; seen by user.  (Save for later restoration.);	ldy #o_ActiveFlag	lda [DAPtr],y	pha	lda #0	sta [DAPtr],y;-------------------------------------------------;; Set notagain flag	to prevent multiple	entries; into CDA menu.;	ldy #o_NotAgain	lda #$8000	sta [DAPtr],y;-------------------------------------------------;; Save current shadow register and set it for; use by CDA menu.;	sep #$30	longa off	longi off	lda >Shadow	pha	and #$FE	; force text shawdow on	sta >Shadow	rep #$30	longa on	longi on;-------------------------------------------------;; Display the CDA menu and run any CDAs.;	jsl CallCDAMenu;-------------------------------------------------;; Restore the shadow register;	sep #$30	longa off	longi off	pla	sta >Shadow	rep #$30	longa on	longi on;-------------------------------------------------;; Restore pointer to global data and restore; the ActiveFlag.  Then clear the NotAgain flag.;	jsr LocalDeref	ldy #o_ActiveFlag	pla	sta [DAPtr],y	ldy #o_NotAgain	lda #0	sta [DAPtr],y;-------------------------------------------------;; Restore original value of KeyInput (from; stack).;	pla	sta >keyinputSkipThisOne		;	lda #$01	; nil means I handled the event	sta result;-----------------------------------------------------;; Restore the NumInts variable from above;	sep #$30	pla	sta >NumInts	rep #$30CannotGoOn	pld	; restore the direct page register	pla	; pull off the 8 bytes used	pla	; for DAHandle and DAPtr	pla	pla	plp	; restore interrupt	status	jml oEndCall16LocalDeref	lda [DAHandle]	sta DAPtr	ldy #2	lda [DAHandle],y	sta DAPtr+2	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** CheckNDAStuff** We look at the event type.  For certain events I pass them* to the Active DA.	 For others, I do not.*****************************************************************	EXPORT CheckNDAStuffCheckNDAStuff	PROC	pld	; restore direct page	pla	; get WAP values back in A & Y	ply	pla	ply	plp	; restore interrupt	state	phy	pha	phy	pha	phd	tsc	tcd;-------------------------------------------------;; Direct page equates until StartNDACall is made.;	DefineStackOrigD	wordDAPtr	longDAHandle	longsret1	block 3sret2	block 3swhat	wordsmessage	longswhen	longswhere	longsmods	wordsresult	word*** added 3-Jan-91 DAL--Apple-W handled by the system	lda <sWhat	cmp #$0005	; is it auto key down?	beq @isKey	cmp #$0003	; is it a key down?	bne @toDoSysEvent@isKey	lda <sMods	and #$0100	; see if the apple key is down...	beq @DoSysEvent	lda <sMessage	and #$00ff	cmp #'w'	beq @DoCloseNDA	cmp #'W'@toDoSysEvent	bne @DoSysEvent@DoCloseNDA*** added 11-Oct-91 DAL -- if Window Manager not here, leave	pea 0	_WindStatus	pla	beq @DoSysEvent*** end 11-Oct-91	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	ply	pla	bne @aWindow	tyx	bne @aWindow	bra @DoSysEvent@aWindow	pha	pha	phy	_GetSysWFlag	pla	bpl @DoSysEvent*** added 12-Dec-91 DAL -- give smart NDAs a chance to handle the fascist Command-W	lda #0	sta >@sysEventBlock	pea 0	;space for CallDeskAcc result	pea $0001	;call NDA Action routine by window pointer	pha	pha	;space for window pointer	_FrontWindow	pea $000B	;action code = handle Command-W	pea @sysEventBlock>>16	pea @sysEventBlock	_CallDeskAcc	plx	;discard	lda >@sysEventBlock	;nonzero = NDA handled it	bne @exitTrue*** end 12-Dec-91	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	_CloseNDAByWinPtr@exitTrue	lda #$ffff	;result = TRUE	bra StoreResult@sysEventBlock	dc.w 0	;12-Dec-91 DAL@DoSysEvent*** end of 3-Jan-91 DAL addition	lda swhat	asl a	; double the event type	tax	; and put in x for later	lda [DAHandle]	sta DAPtr	ldy #2	lda [DAHandle],y	sta DAPtr+2	ldy #o_ActiveFlag	lda [DAPtr],y	bne WeAreActive	lda #0	bra NeverMindWeAreActive	cpx #18	bcc ValidEvent	lda #0	bra NeverMindValidEvent	jsr (EventTable,x)NeverMindStoreResult	sta sResult	pld	; clean up the stack	pla	pla	pla	pla	jml oEndCall16EventTable	DC.W Ignore	; 0  null events	DC.W Ignore	; 1  mouse down	DC.W DoIfWants	; 2  mouse upt	DC.W DoIfWantsKey	; 3  key down	DC.W DoIfWants	; 4  undefined	DC.W DoIfWants	; 5  auto key down	DC.W DoUpdate	; 6  update	DC.W Ignore	; 7  undefined	DC.W DoActivate	; 8  activate	DC.W Ignore	; 9  switch event	DC.W Ignore	; 10 desk acc	DC.W Ignore	; 11 device driver	DC.W Ignore	; 12 Ap	DC.W Ignore	; 13	DC.W Ignore	; 14	DC.W Ignore	; 15;-------------------------------------------------;; Equates for direct page after the startNDACall; is made.; 	DSect OrigDirect+2rtsadr	wordxOrigD	wordxDAPtr	longxDAHandle	longxret1	block 3xret2	block 3Dwhat	wordDmessage	longDwhen	longDwhere	longDmods	wordDresult	wordIgnore	lda #0	rtsDoIfWantsKey; This routine tests the event to see if its a keydown that might have menu implications; If it does this routine will deny that the event belongs to that NDA; This will allow NDA's to handle the cut/copy/paste menu items properly	lda DAHandle	ldy DAHandle+2	jsr StartNDACall	ldy #4	lda [NDAListHandle],y	bpl @1	brl reallyNo@1	jsr DerefNDAList	jsr AreWeTop	bcc No	jsr TestMenuKey	bcc DIW0010	bra no	; if carry set don't handle it! DoIfWants	lda DAHandle	ldy DAHandle+2	jsr StartNDACall	ldy #4	lda [NDAListHandle],y	bmi reallyNo	jsr DerefNDAList	jsr AreWeTop	bcc NoDIW0010	lda Dwhat	asl a	tax	lda >MaskTable,x	ldy #o_EventMask	and [PtrToThisOne],y	bne SendItOnNo	jsr UnlockNDAListReallyNo	jsr EndNDACall	lda #0	rts;----------------------------------------------------; This routine tests the keyboard event for menu keyness...;TestMenuKey	lda Dmods	and #$0100	; see if the apple key is down....;	bne @Keeptrying	clc	; say not menu key...	rts@KeepTrying	; for this release , no command keys for DA's	sec	rts;	lda #$FFFF	; task mask;	ldx #0;	pha;	pha;	phx	; task data;	phx;	pei DMods	; modifiers;	pei Dwhere+2;	pei Dwhere;	pei Dwhen+2;	pei DWhen;	pei DMessage+2;	pei DMessage;	pei DWhat;	tsc	; now get the stack pointer...;	inc a	; bump it by 1..;	phx	; high word of task rec ptr;	pha	; low word of task rec ptr;	phx;	phx;	_MenuKey	; call the menu key routine...;	pla	; yank what;	pla	; yank message;	pla;	pla	; yank When;	pla;	pla	; yank where;	pla;	pla	; yank modifiers;	pla	; yank and save menu item ID;	ply	; get the menu number;	plx	; yank task mask;	plx; Now <A> contains the menu number if any...;	cmp #0;	beq @NDAKey;	pha;	pea 0	; send a false;	phy	; the menu number;	_HiliteMenu	; turn off menu hiliting;	pla;@NotNDAKey	sec	; always pass valid menu keys to the app...;	rts;@NDAKey;	clc;	rts;----------------------------------------------------;; events greater than 9 are not passed on.;MaskTable	DC.W %0000000000000001 ; 0	DC.W %0000000000000010 ; 1	DC.W %0000000000000100 ; 2	DC.W %0000000000001000 ; 3	DC.W %0000000000010000 ; 4	DC.W %0000000000100000 ; 5	DC.W %0000000001000000 ; 6	DC.W %0000000010000000 ; 7	DC.W %0000000100000000 ; 8	DC.W %0000001000000000 ; 9DoActivate		; DoUpdate		; 	lda DAHandle	; set a and y registers before	ldy DAHandle+2	; calling StartNDACall	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	lda DMessage	ldx DMessage+2	jsr FindThisWindow	bcc NoSendItOn	jsr SetResID	tdc	clc	adc #DWhat	tax	ldy #0	lda #DAEventCode	jsl SendAction	jsr RepResID	jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	lda #$8000	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** CallCDAMenu** This routine is almost identical to the daHandle routine* in rom except that we know that we did not get here from* an interrupt so interrupt processing code was removed.** Also, since this is called through system event, we know* that there is no need for scheduling.** This routine is called in full native	mode (the routine* in rom was called	in 8 bit mode).** There is no information returned by this routine.** Change History** 01 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** This routine used	in-line storage to preserve the data* bank.  It now uses the stack.*****************************************************************CallCDAMenu	PROC EXPORT	phb	; save dbr on stack	before anything happens	tsc	; save stack for integer basic	sta >stacksv	phb	; stack is saved as	$E0/0300	ldx #$0100	ldy #$0300	lda #$FF	mvn $000000,$E00000	plb	lda #$1FB	; make sure there's room on stack	tcs	_saveall	; save everything	_choosecda	; display the list of da's	_restall	; unsave everything;               phb		 ; restore stack (but save b);               phb;               pla;               sta	     >LocalBRegSave	ldx #$0300	ldy #$0100	lda #$FF	mvn $E00000,$000000	lda >stacksv	tcs;               lda	     >LocalBRegSave;               pha;               plb;               plb	plb	; restore dbr saved	first thing.	rtl;LocalBRegSave  ds 2	ENDP****************************************************************** InstallNDA**           HandleToNDA** This is the routine we use to install	a new da in the system.* We pass a handle to this call (rather	than a pointer) because* InstallCDA uses a	handle.  (InstallCDA used a handle by* accident and we regret it but there is nothing we can do.)** This call makes a	new entry in the NDAList for the NDA.  This* entry contains most of the information in the NDA header.** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** Changes were made	here to use the new	structure of the * NDAGlobals record.******************************************************************InstallNDA	PROC EXPORT	DSect OrigDirect+2Rtl1	block 3RTL2	block 3UserHandle	long	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	lda [NDAListPtr]	; get the num entries	inc a	pha	; space for result	pha	pha	; Num entries after	adding one	PushWord #NDARecSize ; Size of a NDArecord	_Multiply	lda 1,s	; add result to 2 to get new size	clc	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobals	sta 1,s	bcc SizeIsAdjusted	lda 3,s	inc a	sta 3,sSizeIsAdjusted	lda 1,s	; now calculate where new rec will	sec	sbc #NDARecSize	sta OffsetToThisOne	lda 3,s	sbc #0	sta OffsetToThisOne+2	jsr UnlockNDAList	pei NDAListHandle+2	pei NDAListHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcs ERROR	jsr DerefNDAList;----------------------------------------------------;; Bump the NDA list	count.;	lda [NDAListPtr]	inc a	sta [NDAListPtr]	lda NDAListPtr	clc	adc OffsetToThisOne	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	adc OffsetToThisOne+2	sta PtrToThisOne+2	movelong userhandle,NDAHandle	jsr DerefNDAHandle	lda #0	; zero the status flags (first	sta [PtrToThisOne]	; word of NDA record);----------------------------------------------------;; Move 20 bytes of info from the da to the table.; The NDA offsets are 2 less than the table offsets.;	ldy #0Loop	lda [NDAPtr],y	iny	iny	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	cpy #20	bcc Loop	ldy #o_WindowPtr	; zero the window ptr	lda #0	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	ldy #o_Handle	lda UserHandle	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	lda UserHandle+2	sta [PtrToThisOne],y;; Find the UserID of the handle;	ldy #6		; user id is 6 bytes into handle	lda [UserHandle],y	pha		; save on stack while	pei UserHandle+2		; validating the handle.	pei UserHandle	_CheckHandle	bcc ValidHandle		; handle was valid	lda #0		; handle was not valid, use 0	sta 1,sValidHandle			; put the id into the record	pla	ldy #o_UserID	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	jsr UnlockNDAList	ldx #0GetOut	jsr EndNDACall	jml oErrOut4Error	tax	bra GetOut	ENDP****************************************************************** OpenNDA**     Input     ID : word*     Output    Refnum*** Stack looks like:**      Space For Output*      ID of NDA to	open*      =================*	      <- SP*** The menu manager reserves menu item IDs 1 to 255 for* the system.  I use 1 through NumNDAs for the IDs of* desk accessories.	 When an application wants to open* an NDA, it just calls OpenNDA with the item ID returned* from the menu manager.** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** Changes were made	here to use the new	structure of the * NDAGlobals record.** In addition, I changed the error exit	and normal exit* routines to share	code.*** 16 Jun 88 	Steven Glass** If the NDA returns a NIL window pointer I do not mark it as * being open.  This allows DAs to be modal dialogs and * not be tricky when trying to close.*****************************************************************OpenNDA	PROC EXPORT	DSect OrigDirect+2RTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3ID	wordResult	word	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	lda ID	dec a	cmp [NDAListPtr]	bcc @GotIt	brl NotFound@GotIt	pha	; space for result	pha	; (2 words)	pha	; one less the id of this one	PushWord #NDARecSize	_Multiply	pla	; take result of multply and	plx	; add in the size of the globals	clc	; at the beginning of the handle.	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobals	sta Result	; use this result as the ref num;----------------------------------------------------;; Fix the PtrToThisOne variable using offset just; calculated.;	clc	adc NDAListPTr	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	bcc NoCarry	inc aNoCarry	sta PtrToThisOne+2	lda [PtrToThisOne]	; look at status flags	beq OpenIt	; if zero then not open yet;----------------------------------------------------;; The DA is already	open, so we go and select it.;*** added 2-Jul-92 DAL -- But first, let it handle its own re-open if it wants to	lda #0	sta >@handledReOpen	pha	;space for CallDeskAcc result	pea $0001	;call NDA Action routine by window pointer	ldy #o_WindowPtr+2	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	pha	pea $000C	;action code = handle re-open	pea @handledReOpen>>16	pea @handledReOpen	_CallDeskAcc	plx	;discard	lda >@handledReOpen	bne @handled*** end 2-Jul-92	ldy #o_WindowPtr+2	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	pha	_SelectWindow@handled	brl AllDone@handledReOpen	dc.w 0;----------------------------------------------------;; The DA is not open, so we get it opened.;OpenIt	jsr SetResID*** added 9-Aug-91 DAL -- save the port and set a safe one!	pha	pha	_GetPort	pha	pha	pea 0	pea 4	_GetWAP	plx	pla; Look at $10A on QD Direct page to find the Handle to the First Port	lda >$10A+2,x	pha	lda >$10A,x	pha	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [3],y	tax	lda [3]	sta <3	stx <5	;dereferenced into Port Pointer	pld	_SetPort*** end of 9-Aug-91 DAL	PushLong #0	; put room on stack	jsl SendOpen	; call the open routine	lda 1,s	; if pointer is zero, do nothing more.	ora 3,s	bne @1	pla	pla	bra NoWindow@1	ldy #o_WindowPtr	; put result in windowPtr field	pla	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	pla	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	lda #$8000	; make status word indicate this is	sta [PtrToThisOne]	; open.	pha	; Init the last serviced field 	pha	_GetTick	ldy #o_LastServiced	pla	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	pla	sta [PtrToThisOne],yNoWindow*** added 9-Aug-91 DAL -- restore the port	_SetPort*** end of 9-Aug-91 DAL	jsr RepResID;----------------------------------------------------;; All done, so clean up.AllDone	ldx #0JoinExit	phx	jsr UnlockNDAList	plx	jsr EndNDACall	jml oErrOut2NotFound	ldx #DANotFound	bra JoinExit	ENDP****************************************************************** CloseNDA**     Input     Refnum*** Stack looks like:**      Refnum*      =================*	      <- SP*** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes were needed here to use the new structure of the * NDAGlobals record.******************************************************************CloseNDA	PROC EXPORT	DSect OrigDirect+2RTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3RefNum	word	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	lda NDAListPtr	clc	adc RefNum	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	bcc NoCarry	inc aNoCarry	sta PtrToThisOne+2	lda [PtrToThisOne]	beq NeverMind	jsr DoCloseStuffNeverMind	jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	jml oEndCall2	ENDP****************************************************************** CloseNDAbyWinPtr**     Input     WinPtr*** Stack looks like:**      WinPtr*      =================*	      <- SP**** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes were needed here to use the new structure of the * NDAGlobals record.** However, I changed the error exit and	normal exit* routines to share	code.*****************************************************************CloseNDAbyWinPtr	PROC EXPORT	DSect OrigDirect+2RTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3WinPtr	long	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	lda WinPtr	ldx WinPtr+2	jsr FindThisWindow	bcc CannotFind	jsr DoCloseStuff	ldx #0JoinExit	phx	jsr UnlockNDAList	plx	jsr EndNDACall	jml oErrOut4CannotFind	ldx #NotSysWindow	bra JoinExit	ENDP****************************************************************** CloseAllNDAs**     Input     none*** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes were needed here to use the new structure of the * NDAGlobals record.** However, I changed the code to use the stack to hold a counter* instead of storage in line.*****************************************************************CloseAllNDAs2	PROC EXPORT	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	PushWord #0	; init counter on stack	lda NDAListPtr	clc	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobals	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	bcc NoCarry1	inc aNoCarry1	sta PtrToThisOne+2Loop	lda 1,s	cmp [NDAListPtr]	bcs AllDone	lda [PtrToThisOne]	beq NotOpen	jsr DoCloseStuffNotOpen	lda PtrToThisOne	clc	adc #NDARecSize	sta PtrToThisOne	bcc NoCarry2	inc PtrToThisOne+2NoCarry2;	lda 1,s;	inc a;	sta 1,s	pla	;2-May-91 DAL	inc a	;2-May-91 DAL	pha	;2-May-91 DAL	bra LoopAllDone	pla	; clean off the stack*** added 2-May-91 DAL -- walk the window list, closing non-NDA system windows	pea 0	_WindStatus	pla	beq @noWindows@anotherPass	pha	pha	_GetFirstWindow@nextWindow	lda 2,s	beq @noMoreWindows	pha	;space for GetWKind result	lda 5,s	pha	lda 5,s	pha	;pushed a copy of window pointer	_GetWKind	pla	bpl @advanceToNext@isSysWindow	lda 3,s	pha	lda 3,s	pha	;keep a copy of the window pointer in case Close fails	_CloseNDAByWinPtr	bcs @advanceToNext	pla	pla	bra @anotherPass@advanceToNext	lda 3,s	pha	lda 3,s	pha	;made space for result	_GetNextWindow	bra @nextWindow@noMoreWindows	pla	pla@noWindows*** end of 2-May-91 DAL	jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	jml oEndCall0	ENDP****************************************************************** DoCloseStuff** This is a routine	that is shared by CloseNDA and* by SystemClick for close the NDAs.*** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes required to support new data structures.*****************************************************************DoCloseStuff	PROC EXPORT	jsr SetResID	jsl SendClose	jsr RepResID	ldy #o_WindowPtr	lda #0	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	lda #0	; the the status word	sta [PtrToThisOne]	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** SystemTask** This is the routine that an application must call* periodically to keep desk accessories	alive.  The suggestion* is that applications call this routine every time through* the main event loop.** This routine also	makes the CURSOR calls to the da that* is the front window.** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** Changes were made	here to use the new	structure of the * NDAGlobals record.** Additionally, the	code that reads the	tick count was changed* do turn interrupts off (rather than turning them on) while* the two words are	read.  (The code did a cli rather than* an sei.)*****************************************************************SystemTask	PROC EXPORTTickCount	equ OffsetToThisOne	; zp aliasing*** added 21-Apr-91 DAL -- make SystemTask take no action if GS/OS is busy	tax	lda >$e100be	bpl @1	clc	lda #0	rtl@1	txa*** end of 21-Apr-91 DAL	jsr StartNDACall	;inc busy flag	jsr DerefNDAList	;deref and lock handle to NDAListPtr;------------------------------------------------------;; first send cursor	message if the front window is; one of our windows.;	jsr AreWeTop	;is top window a system window?	bcc NotOnTop	jsr SetResID	lda #DACursorCode	jsl SendAction	jsr RepResID;------------------------------------------------------;; Now go through the list of open DA's and see if; any need periodic	wake upsNotOnTop		; 	ldy #o_TickAddress	; put the address of the tick	lda [NDAListPtr],y	; count on direct page.	sta NDAPtr	iny	iny	lda [NDAListPtr],y	sta NDAPtr+2	php	; ints off while accessing	sei	lda [NDAPtr]	sta TickCount	ldy #2	lda [NDAPtr],y	sta TickCount+2	plp	; restore ints	lda NDAListPtr	; initialize PtrToThisOne	clc	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobals	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	adc #0	sta PtrToThisOne+2	pea 0	; put counter on stackLoop	lda 1,s	; is counter greater or equal num das	cmp [NDAListPtr]	bcs NDAsDone	lda [PtrToThisOne]	; see if it is open	beq NotThisOne	ldy #o_Period	; if period is $FFFF then it	lda [PtrToThisOne],y ; does not want this shit	cmp #$FFFF	beq NotThisOne;------------------------------------------------------;; Calculate how many ticks since last service.;;    TickCount - LastServiced;; If result is negative, invert it (very unlikely since; it takes two years of constant running for the tick; count to wrap.;	lda TickCount	sec	ldy #o_LastServiced	sbc [PtrToThisOne],y	tax	; put result in x	iny	; do rest of divide	iny	lda TickCount+2	sbc [PtrToThisOne],y	bpl IsPos	; if this is pos then it is 0	txa	; if neg then we wrapped.	eor #$FFFF	inc a	taxIsPos	txa	; get back from x and see	ldy #o_Period	; if this is greater than	cmp [PtrToThisOne],y ; period	bcc NotThisOne;------------------------------------------------------;; It is greater than period so save new	value for; last serviced.;	ldy #o_LastServiced	; fix last serviced	field in rec	lda TickCount	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	lda TickCount+2	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	jsr SetResID	lda #DARunCode	; send the run code	to NDA	jsl SendAction	jsr RepResIDNotThisOne	lda PtrToThisOne	; now bump pointer to current da	clc	adc #NDARecSize	sta PtrToThisOne	bcc NoCarry2	inc PtrToThisOne+2NoCarry2	pla	; bump counter on stack	inc a	pha	bra LoopNDAsDone	pla	;remove counter from stack;-----------------------------------------------------------;;  Now check run queue;	ldy #o_TaskQueueHeader ;initialize PtrToThisOne for runQ	lda [NDAListPtr],y	sta PtrToThisOne	iny	iny	lda [NDAListPtr],y	sta PtrToThisOne+2Loop1	lda PtrToThisOne	;check for nil address (end of list)	bne Loop2	lda PtrToThisOne+2	beq AllDoneLoop2	ldy #o_RunPeriod	; if period is $FFFF then it	lda [PtrToThisOne],y ; does not want this shit	cmp #$FFFF	beq SkipThisOne;------------------------------------------------------;; Calculate how many ticks since last service.;;    TickCount - LastServiced;; If result is negative, invert it (very unlikely since; it takes two years of constant running for the tick; count to wrap.;	lda TickCount	sec	ldy #o_RunService	sbc [PtrToThisOne],y	tax	; put result in x	iny	; do rest of divide	iny	lda TickCount+2	sbc [PtrToThisOne],y	bpl IsPos1	; if this is pos then it is 0	txa	; if neg then we wrapped.	eor #$FFFF	inc a	taxIsPos1	txa	; get back from x and see	ldy #o_RunPeriod	; if this is greater than	cmp [PtrToThisOne],y ; period	bcc SkipThisOne;------------------------------------------------------;; It is greater than period so save new	value for; last serviced.;	ldy #o_RunService	; fix last serviced	field in rec	lda TickCount	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	lda TickCount+2	sta [PtrToThisOne],y;Check signature	ldy #o_Signature	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	cmp #Signature	bne SkipthisOne	;signature corrupt: skip it	jsl ExecuteRunItemSkipthisOne	lda [PtrToThisOne]	; now bump pointer to current da	tax	ldy #2	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	sta PtrToThisOne+2	stx PtrToThisOne	bra Loop1	AllDone			jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	jml oEndCall0	ENDP****************************************************************** SystemClick**              PtrToEvent*              PtrToWindow*              ResultFromFindWindow*              ====================*	                <- SP** This is called when an application determines that the mouse* went down in a system window.** It is the job os SystemClick to**      Drag if in DragRegion*      TrackGoAway and close if neccessary if in GoAwayBox*      TrackZoom and zoom if necessary if in ZoomBox*      Grow if in GrowBox*      Select if in	content and not on top or Pass it on*         to the NDA** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes required to support new data structures.  However* a couple of changes were made to save	code.** 15 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Added check for click in grow to select window if not front.** Use FrontToAX instead of inline FrontWindow calls.*****************************************************************SystemClick	PROC EXPORT	DSect OrigDirect+2ret1	block 3	; equates for zp after StartNDACallret2	block 3FindResult	wordWindowPtr	longEventPtr	long*** added 4-Jul-91 DAL -- call CallDeskAcc in case the NDA wants to handle the click	pha	phy	;save for later	lda #0	sta >sysClickBlock	lda 11,s	;FindWindow result;;;	and #$7fff	asl a	lsr a	sta >sysClickBlock+2	lda 13,s	;low word of Window Pointer	sta >sysClickBlock+4	lda 15,s	;high word of Window Pointer	sta >sysClickBlock+6	lda 17,s	;low word of event pointer	sta >sysClickBlock+8	lda 19,s	;high word of event pointer	sta >sysClickBlock+10	pea 0	;space for CallDeskAcc result	pea $0001	;call NDA Action routine by window pointer	lda 15+4,s	pha	lda 15+4,s	pha	;pushed window pointer	pea $000A	;action code = handle SystemClick	pushlong #sysClickBlock  ;data value	_CallDeskAcc	plx	;discard	lda >sysClickBlock	beq sysClickCont	;nonzero result = handled it	ply	pla	;discard saved registers	ldx #0	;no error	ldy #10	;strip 10 bytes	jml $e10184	;ToStripsysClickBlock	dc.w 0	;result	dc.w 0	;FindWindow result (SysClick parm)	dc.l 0	;Window Pointer (SysClick parm)	dc.l 0	;Event Pointer (SysClick parm)sysClickCont	ply	pla*** end of 4-Jul-91 DAL	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	lda FindResult	; in content;;;	and #$7FFF	; mask off the system window bit;;;	sec;;;	sbc #19;;;	asl a*** opt 2-Jul-92 DAL	asl a	sec	sbc #19+19*** end opt	tax	cpx #ClickTableEnd-ClickTable	bcs @ignore	jsr (ClickTable,x)@ignore	jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNdaCall	jml oEndCall10ClickTable	DC.W ClickInContent	; 19	DC.W ClickInDrag	; 20	DC.W ClickInGrow	; 21	DC.W ClickInGoaway	; 22	DC.W ClickInZoom	; 23	DC.W ClickInInfo	; 24	DC.W ClickInVScroll	; 25	DC.W ClickInHScroll	; 26	DC.W ClickInFrame	; 27ClickTableEnd****************************************************************** A click in the content area means one	of two things:**      The da is the top window:   Pass	click on to NDA*      da is not the top window:   Select the sucker.*****************************************************************ClickInContent		; ClickInInfo		; ClickInVScroll		; ClickInHScroll		; ClickInFrame		; 	import FrontToAX;;;PassItAnyway	jsr FrontToAX	cmp WindowPtr	bne SelectIt	cpx WindowPtr+2	bne SelectIt;------------------------------------------------------;; It is top so send	the event on!;	jsr FindThisWindow	bcc ImConfused	jsr SetResID	lda #DAEventCode	ldx EventPtr	ldy EventPtr+2	jsl SendAction	jsr RepResIDImConfused	rtsSelectIt;	PushLong WindowPtr	pei <WindowPtr+2	pei <WindowPtr	_SelectWindow*** added 21-Apr-91 DAL -- if the window frame qContent bit is set, pass it along to the NDA!	pha	pei <WindowPtr+2	pei <WindowPtr	_GetWFrame	pla	and #$0040	;bit 6 = qContent;;;	bne PassItAnyway*** added 4-Dec-91 DAL -- recompute what part of the window it is and make a*** tail-recursive call to SystemClick with the new values	beq @ignoreIt	pei <EventPtr+2	pei <EventPtr	pei <WindowPtr+2	pei <WindowPtr	pha	;space for FindWindow	pea 0	tdc	clc	adc #WindowPtr	;new value not used (we assume it's the same)	pha	ldy #12	;event.where.x	lda [<EventPtr],y	pha	;X value for FindWindow	dey	dey	lda [<EventPtr],y	pha	;Y value for FindWindow	_FindWindow	_SystemClick@ignoreIt*** end 4-Dec-91 DAL*** end of 21-Apr-91 DAL	rtsClickInDrag	ldy #o_modifiers	; if this is shift click	lda [EventPtr],y	; then drag in current plain	and #m_AppleKey	; else bring to top	then drag	bne SkipSelect;------------------------------------------------------;; First see if we are the top window;	jsr FrontToAX	cmp WindowPtr	bne MustSelect	cpx WindowPtr+2	beq SkipSelectMustSelect	jsr SelectItSkipSelect;; 3/16/89	Mensch; Added call to stilldown to be sure that the mouse button state hasn't; changed during the select.	pha	; room for result	pea 00	; button number	_StillDown	; test for it to still be down	pla	beq @Done	; if not still down, then just leave...;; Done with change	PushWord #0	; default grid	ldy #o_Where+2	; where	lda [EventPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [EventPtr],y	pha	PushWord #8	; grace	PushLong #0	; bounds rect (default)	PushLong WindowPtr	_DragWindow@Done	rtsClickInGrow		jsr FrontToAX	cmp WindowPtr	bne toSelectIt	cpx WindowPtr+2	bne toSelectIt	pha	; space for result	pha	jsr PushMinSize	;DAL 4-Mar-91***	PushWord #20	; min x***	PushWord #10	; min y	ldy #o_Where+2	; where x	lda [EventPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [EventPtr],y	; where y	pha	PushLong WindowPtr	; pointer to window	_GrowWindow	PushLong WindowPtr	; don't forget to set the final size	_SizeWindow	rtstoSelectIt	brl SelectIt	;added 4-Dec-91 DAL** PushMinSize -- push 20,10 or the min size from the AuxWindInfo (4-Mar-91 DAL)*PushMinSize	pha	pha	pushlong WindowPtr	_GetAuxWindInfo	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #20	;offset to min height	lda [3],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [3],y	;min width	pld	ply	ply	;min height/width in XA	txy	;zero?	bne @nonzero;;;	ldx #10	;old default height;;;	lda #20	;old default width	ldx #34	;min height (9-Nov-91 DAL)	lda #78	;min width (9-Nov-91 DAL)@nonzero	ply	;pull return address	pha	phx	phy	rtsClickInGoAway	pha	; space for result	ldy #o_Where+2	; where x	lda [EventPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [EventPtr],y	; where y	pha	PushLong WindowPtr	; pointer to window	_TrackGoaway	pla	beq DontClose	lda WindowPtr	ldx WindowPtr+2	jsr FindThisWindow	bcc DontClose	jsr DoCloseStuffDontClose	rtsClickInZoom	PushWord #0	ldy #o_Where+2	; where x	lda [EventPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [EventPtr],y	; where y	pha	PushLong WindowPtr	; pointer to window	_TrackZoom	pla	beq DontZoom	PushLong WindowPtr	_ZoomWindowDontZoom	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** SystemEdit**        Space for boolean result*        Edit Code*        ------------------------*	                <-SP** The application calls this when the user selects cut, copy* paste, undo or clear from the edit menu.  The* user passes the edit code on the stack.** NDA returns boolean in a register.  True if action is* taken, false otherwise.** The Edit codes are**                  Action code send	Code sent to System	Edit*                  to NDA	by application*      Undo	  5	       1*      Cut	  6	       2*      Copy	  7	       3*      Paste	  8	       4*      Clear	  9	       5** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes required to support new data structures.  However* a couple of changes were made to save	code.** 19 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Fixed bug where return code from DA was trashed while * restoring the resource manager's user id.*****************************************************************SystemEdit	PROC EXPORT	import FrontToAX	DSect OrigDirect+2RTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3EditID	wordResult	word	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	stz Result	; start by assuming no!  added 19 Apr 89 SEG	jsr FrontToAX	jsr FindThisWindow	bcc NotOurs	jsr SetResID	lda EditID	; add the edit id number to	clc	; undo code to get right code	adc #DAUndoCode-1	jsl SendAction	; return result in a-reg	sta Result	; Save it now!  added 19 Apr 89 SEG	jsr RepResID	NotOurs		jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	jml oEndCall2	ENDPDieHorribly	PROC EXPORT	rep #$30	lda #BadNDA	and #$00FF	ora #$0500	pha	PushLong #0	_SysFailMgr	EndP****************************************************************** FixAppleMenu2**      input     ID	of menu to add to**      output    none** This is called fix apple menu but, it	can fix any menu* whose id is passed.** Change History** 02 Oct 87	Steven Glass** Changes were needed here to use the new structure of the * NDAGlobals record.** Additionally, I changed the code to use the stack to hold	a counter* instead of storage in line.** 12 Oct 87	Steven Glass** If an error occurs in parsing the menu data, we branch to* die in where the process mode bits are cleared.** 20-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Add sorting option.*****************************************************************FixAppleMenu2	PROC EXPORT	import DieHorribly	DSect OrigDirect+2RTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3WhichMenu	word*** added 16-Sep-91 DAL****** If the Desk Manager is not yet started, try to start it up.  This*** can happen if the application called DeskStartUp too early, so it*** did not start up then. -- If we *still* can't start up, then let's*** don't add any NDA items to the Apple menu.***	pha	phy	;preserve WAP	lda >RealDeskStatus	bne @weAreStarted	_DeskStartUp	lda >RealDeskStatus	bne @weAreStarted	ply	pla	;discard original WAP	ldx #0	;no error	ldy #2	;strip 2 bytes	jml $e10184	;ToStrip@weAreStarted	ply	;restore WAP	pla*** end 16-Sep-91 DAL	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	jsr VerifyBRAM	lda [NDAListPtr]	beq @1	jsr NDASurrogateSort	;added 20-Nov-90 DAL@1	PushWord #0		; init counter on stackInstallLoop	lda 1,s	cmp [NDAListPtr]	bcc Continue	brl AllDoneContinue	jsr SurrogateLookup		;DAL	jsr PointAtNDA		;DAL	jsr DerefThisNDAHandle	;made subroutine 20-Nov-90 DAL;; Now I have to find the H (or h) that appears after; the back slash.;	sep #%00100000	; switch to 8 bit a	reg	longa off	ldy #1	; start with first char@SlashLoop	lda [NDAPtr],y	cmp #'\'	beq @FoundSlash	iny	cpy #255	bcc @SlashLoop	brl DieHorribly		; die horribly if the da is bad@FoundSlash	iny@HLoop	lda [NDAPtr],y	cmp #'H'	beq FoundH	cmp #'h'	beq FoundH	iny	cpy #255	bcc @HLoop	brl DieHorribly		; die horribly if the DA is badFoundH	rep #%00100000	longa on	iny		; put id number into string	lda 1,s		; right after H	phy	jsr surrogateLookup 	ply	inc a	sta [NDAPtr],y	PushLong NDAPtr	PushWord #$FFFF	PushWord WhichMenu	_InsertMItem	pla	inc a	pha	bra InstallLoopAllDone	pla		; clean up stack	lda [NDAListPtr]	beq @1	jsr SurrogateDispose	;DAL 20-Nov-90@1	jsr UnlockNDAList*** added 24-Jul-91 DAL -- call SendRequest(systemSaysFixedAppleMenu)	pea $051E	;systemSaysFixedAppleMenu	ldx #0	phx	;sendHow	phx	phx	;target = nil	phx	phx	;dataIn = nil	phx	phx	;dataOut = nil	_SendRequest*** end 24-Jul-91 DAL	jsr ENDNDACall	jml oEndCall2************************************************************** Made this into a subroutine, 20-Nov-90 DAL** Input:  PtrToThisOne* Output: NDAPtr (points to menu line for NDA)*DerefThisNDAHandle	ldy #o_handle	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	sta NDAhandle	iny	iny	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	sta NDAHandle+2	jsr DerefNDAHandle	lda NDAPtr	clc	adc #20	sta NDAPtr	bcc @NoCarryToLine	inc NDAPtr+2@NoCarryToLine	rts************************************************************************ PointAtNDA (20-Nov-90 DAL)** Input:  A = NDA number (0..NumNDAs-1)** Output:  PtrToThisOne points to our data for this DA*PointAtNDA	pha	pha	;long space for _Multiply result	pha	;input to _Multiply	pea NDARecSize	_Multiply	lda NDAListPtr	clc	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobals	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	bcc @NoCarry1	inc a@NoCarry1	sta PtrToThisOne+2	pla	;add on the result of the _Multiply	clc	adc PtrToThisOne	sta PtrToThisOne	pla	adc PtrToThisOne+2	sta PtrToThisOne+2	rts************************************************************************ NDASurrogateSort* 20-Nov-90 DAL** Allocates*NDASurrogateSort	pha	pha	;space for NewHandle	pea 0	;size high	lda [<NDAListPtr]	;number of NDAs	asl a	;  times 2	pha	;size low	pea $5001	;id	pea $8000	;attributes	pha	pha	_NewHandle	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [3],y	sta >SurrogatePtr+2	lda [3]	sta >SurrogatePtr	pld	pla	sta >SurrogateHandle	pla	sta >SurrogateHandle+2*** Initialize the surrogate array to linear list:  a[n]=n	lda [<NDAListPtr]	;number of NDAs	dec a	;minus one	tax	phd	pushlong >SurrogatePtr	tsc	tcd	txa	asl a	tay	txa@init	sta [1],y	dey	dey	dec a	bpl @init	ply	ply	pld	pha	;space for result	pea $5f	;toolbox misc parameter	_ReadBParam	pla	lsr a	bcc @noSortDA	;bit 0 clear = don't sort*** do the sort	phb	phk	plb	lda [<NDAListPtr]	dec a	beq @sorted@OutBubble	stz sortIndex	stz swappedFlag@InBubble	jsr compareTwo	bcc @ordered	ror swappedFlag	jsr swapTwo@ordered	inc sortIndex	lda sortIndex	inc a	cmp [<NDAListPtr]	bcc @InBubble	lda swappedFlag	bne @OutBubble@sorted	plb@noSortDA	rtssortIndex	dc.w 0swappedFlag	dc.w 0************************************************************************ compareTwo** Compare the sortIndex-th NDA name with the (sortIndex+1)th NDA* name.  Return CLC if they are already properly ordred.*compareTwo	phd	lda sortIndex	inc a	jsr GetNamePointer	;into XA	phx	pha	lda sortIndex	jsr GetNamePointer	;into XA	phx	pha	tsc	tcd** compare "\"-terminated string at [1] string at [5]	sep #$30	longa off	longi off	ldy #0@compare	lda [1],y	cmp #'\'	;moved from below 30-Nov-90 DAL (to not hang with identical names)	beq @lesser	;moved from below 30-Nov-90 DAL	lda [5],y	cmp #'\'	beq @greater	jsr upcase	sta @cheat+1	lda [1],y;;;;	cmp #'\'	;moved above 30-Nov-90 DAL;;;;	beq @lesser	;moved above 30-Nov-90 DAL	jsr upcase@cheat	cmp #$77	bne @done	iny	bra @compare@lesser	clc	bra @done@greater	sec@done	rep #$30	longa on	longi on	ply	ply	ply	ply	pld	rts************************************************************************ upcase*	longa offupcase	cmp #'a'	bcc @1	cmp #'z'+1	bcs @1	and #$DF@1	rts	longa on************************************************************************ GetNamePointer** Input:  A,  D=desk manager stuff** Output: XA = pointer to NDA's PString name*GetNamePointer	jsr SurrogateLookup	jsr PointAtNDA	jsr DerefThisNDAHandle* skip past two boring leading bytes plus any leading blanks	ldy #1@skipblanks	iny	lda [<NDAPtr],y	and #$00ff	cmp #$0020	beq @skipblanks	clc	tya	adc NDAPtr	ldx NDAPtr+2	rts************************************************************************ swapTwo** Swaps the sortIndex-th and (sortIndex+1)th surrogate entries.** Inputs:  SurrogatePtr, sortIndex.** The bank register must be set.* Trashes Y.*swapTwo	lda sortIndex	asl a	tay	phd	lda SurrogatePtr+2	pha	lda SurrogatePtr	pha	tsc	tcd	lda [1],y	pha	;save first value	iny	iny	lda [1],y	;get 2nd value	dey	dey	sta [1],y	;put it in first location	iny	iny	pla	;put old first value into 2nd location	sta [1],y	ply	ply	pld	rts** SurrogateLookup* 20-Nov-90 DAL** Input:  A = position in surrogate-sort array* Output: A = NDA number** Looks up an NDA number from a position index** Trashes Y.*SurrogateLookup	asl a	tay	phd	lda >SurrogatePtr+2	pha	lda >SurrogatePtr	pha	tsc	tcd	lda [1],y	ply	ply	pld	rts** SurrogateDispose* 20-Nov-90 DAL*SurrogateDispose	pushlong >SurrogateHandle	_DisposeHandle	rtsSurrogateHandle	dc.l 0SurrogatePtr	dc.l 0** VerifyBRAM -- if the toolbox misc location isn't initialized,*               give it a nice default value.** We have to do this because it defaults to 0 on ROM 1 and* $ff on ROM 3.*	entry VerifyBRAMVerifyBRAM	pha	pea $5f	_ReadBParam	pla	and #%11000000	cmp #%10000000	beq @okay	pea $81	;Initialize toolbox location to default value ($81)	pea $5F	_WriteBParam@okay	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** GetNumNDAs**     Input     none*     Output    number*** Stack looks like:**      Space For Output*      =================*	      <- SP*** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes were needed here to use the new structure of the * NDAGlobals record.** I changed the equates to use DSect macros.** 23 Mar 88	Steven Glass** There was a space in definition of DSect causing equs to be* wrong.*****************************************************************GetNumNDAs	PROC EXPORT	DSect OrigDirect+2RTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3Result	word	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	lda [NDAListPtr]	sta Result	jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	jml oEndCall0	ENDP****************************************************************** SystemMenu** This is not really a call that anyone	can use.** Removed by Steven	Glass* 02 Oct 87*****************************************************************	title 'Desk Manager--desk/DESK.UTILS';               copy desk/desk.utils****************************************************************** Desk Utility Routines** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** Changes were made	to get these to work with new global data* structures.  The DerefNDAHandle routine no longer* locks the handle (we assume that it is already locked)** UnlockNDAHandle was removed (it was never called).** A number of start/end's were combined into one.******************************************************************DeskUtils	PROC EXPORT;----------------------------------------------------;; DerefNDAList;; Locks the NDAListHandle and deref's it into; NDAListPtr		EXPORT DerefNDAListDerefNDAList	lda >EntryCount	inc a	sta >EntryCount	ldy #4	lda [NDAListHandle],y	ora #$8000	;lock the handle	sta [NDAListHandle],y	dey	dey	lda [NDAListHandle],y	sta NDAListPtr+2	lda [NDAListHandle]	sta NDAListPtr	rts;----------------------------------------------------;; UnlockNDAList;; Unlocks the NDAList handle.	EXPORT UnlockNDAListUnlockNDAList	lda >EntryCount	dec a	sta >EntryCount	bne LeaveItLocked	ldy #4	lda [NDAListHandle],y	and #$7FFF	sta [NDAListHandle],yLeaveItLocked	rts;----------------------------------------------------;; DerefNDAHandle;; Derefs but does not bother locking the handle to; the NDA.;	EXPORT DerefNDAHandle DerefNDAHandle	ldy #2	lda [NDAHandle],y	sta NDAPtr+2	lda [NDAHandle]	sta NDAPtr	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** FindThisWindow** Inputs*       a-reg:  low	word of window ptr to look for*       x-reg:  high word of window ptr to look for** Outputs:*   carry:  set if window is found*           clear if window is not found*   DPage:*     OffsetToThisOne & PtrToThisOne set to point into*     global data.** We search through	the NDAList for an NDA with a window ptr* equal to the one passed in the a and x register.** If we find it, we	return with the carry set and the* variables OffsetToThisOne and PtrToThisOne set on zero page.** If we do not find	it we return with carry clear.** * Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** Changes were made	to get this to work	with new global data* structures.*****************************************************************FindThisWindow	PROC EXPORT	phx	; store the pointer	on the stack	pha	;*** added 19-Feb-91 DAL	sta >DeskGlobalWindow	txa	sta >DeskGlobalWindow+2*** end of 19-Feb-91 DAL	ldy #SizeOfDeskGlobals ; y points to first NDA record	ldx #1	; x is countKeepLooking	txa	; compare count to num scrap records	cmp [NDAListPtr]	beq LastItem	bcs NotInTableLastItem	tya	clc	adc #o_WindowPtr	tay	lda [NDAListPtr],y	; get the type of this scrap record	iny	; bump y before compare	iny	cmp 1,s	; compare to value on stack	bne NotThisOne	lda [NDAListPtr],y	cmp 3,s	beq FoundItNotThisOne	tya	; bump y by size of	record	clc	; minus what we've already bumped	adc #NDARecSize-o_WindowPtr-2	tay	inx	; bump count by 1	bra KeepLookingFoundIt	pla	; clear pointer off	stack	pla	tya	; fix Offset To this one by subtracting	sec	; off the extra we just added to get to	sbc #o_WindowPtr+2	; window ptr.	sta OffsetToThisOne	stz OffsetToThisOne+2	lda NDAListPtr	clc	adc OffsetToThisOne	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	adc OffsetToThisOne+2	sta PtrToThisOne+2	sec	rts*** 19-Feb-91 DAL*** Call GetAuxWindInfo and grab a pointer to the NDA-like structure from there, if any.*** Window pointer is still on stack.NotInTable	plx	pla	phy	phy	;space for GetAuxWindInfo result	pha	phx	;pushed window pointer;	pha	;space for GetWKind result;	pha;	phx	;pushed second copy of window pointer;	_GetWKind;	pla;	bpl @appWindow*** 16-Apr-91 DAL -- calling GetWKind trashes some WM direct page, so look in the record directly*** (the system-window bit is bit 31 of the window's port's pixelMap pointer!)	phd	pha	phx	tsc	tcd	ldy #4	lda [1],y	plx	plx	pld	tax	bpl @appWindow*** end of 16-Apr-91 DAL	_GetAuxWindInfo	pla	plx	bcs @notfound	phd	phx	pha	tsc	tcd	ldy #24	;offset into aux wind info of NDAStruct	lda [1],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [1],y	;NDAStruct pointer in AX	ply	ply	pld	tay	bne @found	txy	beq @notfound@found	sta <PtrToThisOne+2	;not nil--return it in PtrToThisOne	stx <PtrToThisOne	stz <OffsetToThisOne	stz <OffsetToThisOne+2	;make sure nobody's using this!	sec	rts@appWindow	pla	pla	pla	pla@notfound	clc	rts	export DeskGlobalWindowDeskGlobalWindow	dc.l 0	ENDP****************************************************************** AreWeTop** Decides if the top window is a system	window.  If it is* then AreWeTop returns with carry set.	 If the top window* is not a system window, then AreWeTop	returns with carry* clear.** Additionally, if the window is a system window, I call* find this window which sets up PtrToThisOne.  FindThisWindow* must also succeed	for AreWeTop to return true.*** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No changes were needed for new data structures but* I changed a PushLong #0 to pha pha to	save space.** 15 mar 89	Steven Glass** Uses FrontToAX instead of calling FrontWindow directly* saving lots of code.** Also branch directly to FindThisWindow rather than* jsr followed by rts.  This saves more code.*****************************************************************AreWeTop	PROC EXPORT	jsr FrontToAX	tay	bne FindthisWindow0	txy	bne FindThisWindow0NotSystem	clc	rtsFindThisWindow0	brl FindThisWindow	;DAL	ENDP*****************************************************************FutzResIDs	proc** Two routines here are used to set and restore the Resource* Manager's current Resource App.** These calls are meant to be made around calls to the* NDA.  Example:**	jsr SetResID*	send msg to NDA*	jsr RepResID** The first call puts the current resID on the stack,* The second call pulls it off.*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:	Export SetResID	Export RepResID*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 01 Mar 89	Steven Glass & Harry Yee** Harry scolds steve and tells him that you cannot call the * resource manager and expect it to work, if the resource * manager is not there.** No disk other that 4.1 worked at all.*****************************************************************SetResID	plx	; make room on the stack above	pha	; the rts	phx	pea 0	; call resource status	_ResourceStatus	pla	; get result in a-reg	bcs @Done	; carry set means got dispatch error	beq @Done	; 0 means resource manager not active	pha	; get the current res app id	_GetCurResourceApp	pla	sta 3,s	; put it on the stack above the RTS	ldy #o_UserID	; set the id of the NDA about to be called	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	pha	_SetCurResourceApp@Done	rts	; done	RepResID	plx	; pull off the old ID and put back	pla	phx	; the rts addr	pha	; save id on this side of rts adr	pea 0	; call status	_ResourceStatus	pla	; get status result	plx	; get id off stack	tay	; set the zero bit of processor	bcs @Done	beq @Done	phx	; push id now in x-reg	_SetCurResourceApp@Done	rts	; done.	ENDP*****************************************************************SendOpen	PROC EXPORT** This routine transfers control to the	open routine of the* DA pointed to by PointerToThisOne.  All registers and* relative stack locations are preserved.  Control returns* from the DA to the Calling routine, not here.**** Inputs:*	a, x and y are all passed on to the NDA*	unchanged.** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:	ENTRY SendSomething*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No chnages were necessary to support the new data structures.** 19 Feb 89	Steven Glass** All the send routines ended the same way, so they now * share code with SendOpen.  The new entry point is SendSomething.*****************************************************************s_YReg	equ 1s_AReg	equ 3s_AdrForOpen	equ 5	pha	; put 3 bytes on stack	phb	; for addr of action routine	pha	; save a	phy	; save y	ldy #o_Open+1	; get addr from tableSendSomething	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	sta s_AdrForOpen+1,s	dey	lda [PtrToThisOne],y ; rtl adds 1 so sub 1	dec a	sta s_AdrForOpen,s	ply	pla	rtl	ENDP****************************************************************** SendClose** This routine transfers control to the	close routine of the* DA pointed to by PointerToThisOne.  All registers and* relative stack locations are preserved.  Control returns* from the DA to the Calling routine, not here.**** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No chnages were necessary to support the new data structures.*****************************************************************SendClose	PROC EXPORTs_YReg	equ 1s_AReg	equ 3s_AdrForClose	equ 5	pha	; put 3 bytes on stack	phb	; for addr of action routine	pha	; save a	phy	; save y	ldy #o_Close+1	; get addr from table	bra SendSomething	ENDP****************************************************************** SendInit** This routine transfers control to the	init routine of the* DA pointed to by PointerToThisOne.  All registers and* relative stack locations are preserved.  Control returns* from the DA to the Calling routine, not here.**** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No chnages were necessary to support the new data structures.*****************************************************************SendInit	PROC EXPORTs_YReg	equ 1s_AReg	equ 3s_AdrForInit	equ 5	pha	; put 3 bytes on stack	phb	; for addr of action routine	pha	; save a	phy	; save y	ldy #o_Init+1	; get addr from table	bra SendSomething	ENDP****************************************************************** SendAction** Inputs*    All-registers*    PtrToThisOne** Output*    Depends on routine called.** This routine transfers control to the	action routine of the* DA pointed to by PointerToThisOne.  All registers and* relative stack locations are preserved.  Control returns* from the DA to the Calling routine, not here.*** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** No chnages were necessary to support the new data structures.*****************************************************************SendAction	PROC EXPORTs_YReg	equ 1s_AReg	equ 3s_AdrForAction	equ 5	pha	; put 3 bytes on stack	phb	; for addr of action routine	pha	; save a	phy	; save y*** 26-Jun-92 DAL -- Add stack-based dispatch option.  Set bit 31 of action pointer.;	ldy #o_Action+1	; get addr from table;;	bra SendSomething;;SendSomething	lda [PtrToThisOne],y;	sta s_AdrForOpen+1,s;	dey;	lda [PtrToThisOne],y ; rtl adds 1 so sub 1;	dec a;	sta s_AdrForOpen,s;;	ply;	pla;;	rtl	ldy #o_Action+2	; get address from table	lda [<PtrToThisOne],y	bmi @stack_dispatch	dey	; Y = o_Action+1	bra SendSomething	; old way*** A = code, YX = data value (sometimes event pointer)@stack_dispatch	ply	pla*** strip 3 extra bytes off stack (we pushed them at beginning of SendAction)	sta 2,s	phb	pla	pla	pea 0	;push result space	pha	;action code	phy	phx	;data/pointer	jsl @jump_action	pla	;get result into A	rtl@jump_action	ldy #o_Action+1	lda [<PtrToThisOne],y	pha	phb	dey	lda [<PtrToThisOne],y	dec a	sta 1,s	rtl*** end 26-Jun-92	ENDP****************************************************************** StartNDACall** Inputs:*    A-reg:  Low word of WAP value*    Y-reg:  High word of WAP value** Outputs*    D-reg:  set to	place on stack*    b-reg:  set to	code bank (k)*    a-reg, x-reg and y-reg are trashed.** Side Effects:**    busy flag is incremented.*** This routine sets	up direct page, adjusts the stack and* data bank, calls IncBusyFlag in preperation for the* start of a NDA Calls.** It also leaves the WAP value (the handle to the global* data structure) in the NDAListHandle field on direct page.**** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** Changes were necessary to support the new data structures.  The* A & Y registers contain the WAP value	for this tool.*****************************************************************StartNDACall	PROC EXPORT	plx	; get rts adr in x	phd	; save direct reg	phy	; this is the handle to the	pha	; global data structure.	tsc	; and get my zero page off stack	sec	sbc #StdZPSize-4	tcs	tcd	phb	; save data bank	phk	; set data bank to	plb	; code bank	jsl IncBusyFlg	phx	; put rts adr back on stack	rts	ENDP****************************************************************** EndNDACall** Inputs:*     None** Outputs:*     None, but the	x-register is preserved!** This routine restores direct page and	data bank, and adjusts* the stack and calls DecBusyFlg to undo everything that * StartNDACall did.**** Change History** 02 Oct 87	    Steven Glass** Changes were made	to support the new data structures.  This * routine now undoes everything done by	the StartNDACall including* the busyflag and the direct page.*****************************************************************EndNDACall	PROC EXPORT	ply	; save rts adr in y	plb	; restore data bank	tsc	; adjust stack	clc	adc #StdZPSize	tcs	pld	; restore direct page	phy	; put rts back on stack	jsl DecBusyFlg	rts	ENDP************************************************************************ AddToRunQ**  Written by Konstantin Othmer  Sept 29 88** Adds a task to the run queue.  *  Input:*    HeaderPtr	LONG	;address of routine to add**  Output:*    None	***********************************************************************AddToRunQ	PROC EXPORTPtrToHeader	equ FirstInput 	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	;set up NDAListPtr	pei PtrToHeader+2	pei PtrToHeader	lda NDAListPtr	clc	adc #o_TaskQueueHeader	tax	lda NDAListPtr+2	adc #0	pha	phx;	_AddToQueue	;this needs to be made into a macro	ldx #AddToQueue	jsl Dispatch1	tax	jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	jml oErrOut4		ENDP************************************************************************ RemoveFromRunQ**  Written by Konstantin Othmer  Sept 29 88** Removes a task from the run queue.  *  Input:*    HeaderPtr	LONG	;address of routine to add**  Output:*    None	***********************************************************************RemoveFromRunQ	PROC EXPORTPtrToHeader	equ FirstInput	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	;set up NDAListPtr	pei PtrToHeader+2	pei PtrToHeader	lda NDAListPtr	clc	adc #o_TaskQueueHeader	tax	lda NDAListPtr+2	adc #0	pha	phx;	_DeleteFromQueue	;this needs to be made into a macro	ldx #DeleteFromQueue	jsl Dispatch1	tax	jsr UnlockNDAList	jsr EndNDACall	jml oErrOut4		ENDP****************************************************************** ExecuteRunItem** Inputs*    PointerToThisOne** Output*    Depends on RunQ item** This routine transfers control to PointerToThisOne + RunEntry.* All registers and relative stack locations are preserved.* Control returns from the run item to the Calling routine, not here.*** Added by:** Konstantin Othmer		02 Oct 88	    *****************************************************************ExecuteRunItem	PROC EXPORTs_YReg	equ 1s_AReg	equ 3s_AdrForAction	equ 5	;stack + 5 has low byte	pha	; put 3 bytes on stack	phb	; for addr of action routine	pha	; save a	phy	; save y	lda PtrToThisOne+1	;high byte and PCBank	sta s_AdrForAction+1,s ;high byte and PCBank	lda #o_RunEntry	; Code starts here	clc	adc PtrToThisOne	dec a	sta s_AdrForAction,s ;low and high byte return address	ply	pla	rtl	;jump to RunEntry	ENDP	****************************************************************** RemoveNDA**           HandleToNDA** This is the routine we use to remove a new da in the system.** This call removes an entry in the NDAList.  This* entry contains most of the information in the NDA header.** Change History** 05 Oct 88	    Added by Konstantin Othmer*****************************************************************RemoveNDA	PROC EXPORT	import DerefNDAList	import UnlockNDAList	DSect OrigDirect+2Rtl1	block 3RTL2	block 3UserHandle	long	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList	;this locks the handle	;First set up PtrToThisOne to first NDA in the list	lda #SizeofDeskGlobals	clc	adc NDAListPtr	sta PtrToThisOne	lda NDAListPtr+2	adc #0	sta PtrToThisOne+2		lda [NDAListPtr]	;number of entries	pha		;Scan list to try to find UserHandle in the o_Handle field of the NDAList.SearchLoop	pla	beq NotFound	dec a	;keep track of number left to search	pha		ldy #o_Handle	lda UserHandle	cmp [PtrToThisOne],y	bne Search1	iny	iny	lda UserHandle+2	cmp [PtrToThisOne],y	bne Search1	bra FoundIt;	; Didn't find it yet.  Set up PtrtoThisOne for next NDA record and search again;Search1	lda PtrToThisOne	clc	adc #NDARecSize	sta PtrToThisOne	lda PtrToThisOne+2	adc #0	sta PtrToThisOne+2	bra SearchLoop;;found it.  Now we need to remove it.  All the remaining NDA's move up 20 bytes; Top word on stack contains the number of NDAs left in list (not including this one);FoundIt	lda [NDAListPtr]	;number of NDAs:  decrement because	dec a	;we remove one	sta [NDAListPtr]	bra enterMoveStart	lda PtrToThisOne	;Bump ptrtothisone so we can copy the next	ldx PtrToThisOne+2	;NDA to its proper place in the list.	clc	adc #NDARecSize	bcc @nocarry	inx@nocarry	sta PtrToThisOne	stx PtrToThisOne+2enter	pla	;number of NDA's left to search/move	beq SizeHandle	;is this the last one?	dec a	pha	;This now is the number of NDA's we need to		;move;;move record at PtrToThisOne+NDARecSize to PtrToThisOne;	ldx #NDARecSize-2	;length of record to move	ldy #NDARecSize*2-2	;end of source	MoveIt	lda [PtrToThisOne],y	phy	phx	ply	;transfer destination offset to y	sta [PtrToThisOne],y	ply	;get y back	dey	dey	dex	dex	;update offsets	cpx #-2	bne MoveIt	bra MoveStart;; this is inserted here so we can use a short branch to get to itNotFound	ldx #daNotFound	;Not found Error	bra GetOut; end of insert	;	; We've removed it.  Now free up extra room w/ memory manager;SizeHandle	pha	; space for result	pha	lda [NDAListPtr]	;new number of NDAs	pha	; New Number of entries 	PushWord #NDARecSize ; Size of a NDArecord	_Multiply	lda 1,s	; This is size of all NDA Records	clc	;now add in the header size (Deskglobals)	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobalsSizeIsAdjusted	sta 1,s	lda 3,s	adc #0		sta 3,s	;top of stack contains new handle size	jsr UnlockNDAList	pei NDAListHandle+2	pei NDAListHandle	_SetHandleSize	bcs ERRORAllDone	ldx #0	;Successful removalGetOut	jsr EndNDACall	jml oErrOut4Error	tax	;Handle Error	bra GetOut	ENDP****************************************************************** $2305 GetDeskAccInfo** New call for 6.0   11-Mar-91 DAL** Inputs:*    WORD  flags*            bit 15: 0=call NDA, 1=call CDA*            bits 14-1: reserved*            bit  0: 0=daReference is index, 1=NDA window pointer*    LONG  DA Reference (index number or window pointer)*    WORD  buffer size in bytes*    LONG  buffer pointer** In the buffer, the first word returned is the number of bytes* of valid data that follow.*****************************************************************	longa on	; mode	longi onGetDeskAccInfo	PROC EXPORT	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList@buffer	equ FirstInput@buffSize	equ @buffer+4@daReference	equ @buffSize+2@flags	equ @daReference+4@temp	equ PtrToThisOne	lda <@flags	bmi @CDAinfo@NDAinfo	lsr a	;bit 0: 1 for window pointer	bcs @byWindow	lda <@daReference	beq @invalid0	dec a	cmp [<NDAListPtr]	bcs @invalid0	pha	pha	;space for Multiply result	pha	;NDA number	pea NDARecSize	_Multiply	clc	lda <NDAListPtr	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobals	sta <PtrToThisOne	lda <NDAListPtr+2	adc #0	sta <PtrToThisOne+2	clc	pla	adc <PtrToThisOne	sta <PtrToThisOne	pla	adc <PtrToThisOne+2	sta <PtrToThisOne+2	bra @copyInfo@invalid0	bra @invalid@byWindow	ldx <@daReference+2	lda <@daReference	jsr FindThisWindow	bcc @invalid@copyInfo	lda <@buffSize	cmp #4	bcc @invalid	cmp #NDARecSize	bcc @thisMuch	lda #NDARecSize@thisMuch	sta [<@buffer]	tay@copyStuff	dey	dey	lda [<ptrToThisOne],y	iny	iny	sta [<@buffer],y	dey	dey	bne @copyStuff	bra @noProblem@CDAinfo	lda <@buffSize	cmp #4	bcc @buffTooSmall	lda <@daReference	beq @invalid	dec a	cmp >NumDAs	bcs @invalid	asl a	asl a	pha	lda >CDATabHndl+2	sta <@temp+2	lda >CDATabHndl	sta <@temp	ldy #2	lda [<@temp],y	tax	lda [<@temp]	sta <@temp	stx <@temp+2	ply	lda [<@temp],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [<@temp],y	ldy #4	sta [<@buffer],y	dey	dey	txa	sta [<@buffer],y	lda #4	sta [<@buffer]@noProblem	ldx #0	bra @exit@buffTooSmall	ldx #$054F	;dmBufferTooSmall	bra @exit@invalid	ldx #$0520	;bad input value@exit	phx	jsr UnlockNDAList	plx	jsr EndNDACall	ldy #12	jml $e10184	;ToStrip	EndP****************************************************************** $2405 CallDeskAcc** New call for 6.0   11-Mar-91 DAL** Inputs:*   WORD  space for result*   WORD  flags*           bit 15: 0=call NDA, 1=call CDA*           bit 1: call the Init routine instead of Action (NDA)*           bit 0: 0=daReference is index, 1=window pointer*   LONG  daReference (index or window pointer)*   WORD  action code*   LONG  data to pass to NDA*****************************************************************	longa on	; mode	longi onCallDeskAcc	PROC EXPORT	jsr StartNDACall	jsr DerefNDAList@data	equ FirstInput@action	equ @data+4@daReference	equ @action+2@flags	equ @daReference+4@result	equ @flags+2@temp	equ PtrToThisOne	stz <@result	lda <@flags	bpl @callNDA	brl @callCDA@callNDA	lsr a	;bit 0: 1 for window pointer	bcs @byWindow	lda <@daReference	beq @invalid0	dec a	cmp [<NDAListPtr]	bcc @ok@invalid0	brl @invalid@ok	pha	pha	;space for Multiply result	pha	;NDA number	pea NDARecSize	_Multiply	clc	lda <NDAListPtr	adc #SizeOfDeskGlobals	sta <PtrToThisOne	lda <NDAListPtr+2	adc #0	sta <PtrToThisOne+2	clc	pla	adc <PtrToThisOne	sta <PtrToThisOne	pla	adc <PtrToThisOne+2	sta <PtrToThisOne+2	bra @callTheNDA@byWindow	ldx <@daReference+2	lda <@daReference	jsr FindThisWindow	bcc @invalid@callTheNDA	lda <@flags	and #2	bne @callNDAInit	ldy #o_EventMask	lda [<PtrToThisOne],y	and #$f000	cmp #$a000	beq @eatsAnything	lda <@action	cmp #10	bcs @invalid@eatsAnything	jsr SetResID	lda <@action	ldy <@data+2	ldx <@data	jsl SendAction	;A=action, YX=data	sta <@result	jsr RepResID	bra @noProblem@callNDAInit	ldy #o_EventMask	lda [<PtrToThisOne],y	and #$f000	cmp #$a000	beq @eatAnything2	lda <@action	cmp #2	bcs @invalid@eatAnything2	jsr SetResID	lda <@action	ldy <@data+2	ldx <@data	jsl SendInit	sta <@result	jsr RepResID	bra @noProblem@callCDA	bra @invalid@noProblem	ldx #0	bra @exit@invalid	ldx #$0520	;bad input value@exit	phx	jsr UnlockNDAList	plx	jsr EndNDACall	ldy #12	jml $e10184	;ToStrip	EndP****************************************************************** $2505 GetDeskGlobal** Inputs:*    LONG space for result*    WORD selector** Selector values:*    0 = return the current window pointer (to be used*        when an Action proc gets called, in case the*        same action proc is shared among multiple windows)** New call for 6.0   19-Feb-91 DAL*****************************************************************GetDeskGlobal	proc export	import DeskGlobalWindowselector	equ 7	;stackresult	equ selector+2	ldx #$0520	;bad input value	lda selector,s	bne @error	lda >DeskGlobalWindow	sta result,s	lda >DeskGlobalWindow+2	sta result+2,s	ldx #0@error	ldy #2	;strip 2 bytes	jml >$e10184	;ToStrip*****************************************************************FrontToAX	PROC export** Returns the pointer to the front window to in the A & X * registers.*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	a-reg*	x-reg** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	pla	plx	rts	ENDP	END